==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|it|passacaglia}}, from {{der|en|es|pasacalle}}, from {{m|es|pasar||to pass}} + {{m|es|calle||street}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˌpasəˈkɑːlɪ.ə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌpɑsəˈkɑljə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|music genre}} A form of [[historical]] [[Spanish]] or [[Italian]] [[dance]] characterised by a serious nature, [[triple metre]], and use of a [[ground bass]].
# {{lb|en|music|by extension}} Any piece of [[classical music]] with similar characteristics.

